  <h2 id="before-you-start">What to have ready before you sign up</h2>
  <p>
    Most electricians get stuck at signup for weeks, sometimes months. Nearly every time, it is
    because paperwork did not match. Get these together first and it goes smoothly.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Your insurance certificate</strong> as a PDF or clear photo
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Your electrical licence</strong>, photographed, for every state or area you claim
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Your business name and address, exactly as they appear on those documents.</strong>
      One letter off and Google rejects you without saying why.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>A Google Business Profile</strong> (your listing on Google Maps) with at least five
      reviews and “Electrician” set as the main category
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>The owner’s name and email</strong> for a background check
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>A credit card</strong> with enough limit to cover the budget you will set
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="sign-up">Signing up and getting the green tick</h2>
  <p>
    Sit down at a computer, not your phone. Go to
    <a href="https://business.google.com/us/ad-solutions/local-service-ads/">Google’s Local Services
    Ads page</a>, sign in with the Google account that owns your Business Profile, and click
    <strong>Get started</strong>.
  </p>
  <figure>
    <Picture
      name="lsa-signup-get-started"
